"""aera-gateway - sets up the AERA gateways on a Raspberry Pi (or any
Debian, Ubuntu or Raspberry Pi OS computer), brings them up to date and
says how they are.

  sudo ./aera-gateway install mail IMAP SMTP[:587] [POP3]   EMail's (emailgate)
  sudo ./aera-gateway install dav                           ECal's and EContact's (ecalgate)
  sudo ./aera-gateway install ftp                           EFTP's (eftpgate)
  sudo ./aera-gateway install web                           EWeb's (webgate)
  sudo ./aera-gateway install claude --network --atari ATARI_IP
                                                            ClaudeST's bridge (claude-st)
  sudo ./aera-gateway install all --allow ATARI_IP --mail IMAP SMTP[:587] [POP3] [--browser]
                                                            all of them at once
  sudo ./aera-gateway update        every one installed, from this copy, settings kept
                                    (../update-pi.sh: this copy to the latest release first)
  aera-gateway status               what runs, on which ports, with which settings
  sudo ./aera-gateway remove SERVICE
  sudo ./aera-gateway set-key       a new claude.ai session key for ClaudeST

`aera-gateway install SERVICE --help` lists a service's settings. Run
install again to change some of them: the others stay as they are.

A gateway set up by an app's own install.sh (EMail, ECal or EFTP before
the gateways moved here) is taken over by `update` or `install`: the
same service, user, ports and settings, the old copy removed only once
the new one answers.
"""

